<parametername direction="in">lhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Left hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">rhs</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Right hand side operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A logical conjunction object that evaluates to true if both operands are true.</para>
</simplesect>
This overload of the logical <computeroutput>&amp;&amp;</computeroutput> (and) operator enables conjunction between two operands, where at least one is a local type derived from the local <computeroutput>op</computeroutput> base. It constructs a logical conjunction object that can be used within the µTest++ framework to assert that both operands evaluate to true. This operator is intended for use with the framework&apos;s strongly-typed constants, wrappers, or other custom types, ensuring type-safe and expressive test assertions. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
